There are 2 lawful artifacts that non-lawfuls can get with patience
and deep exploration: The ones that 5% of A's get.  Play extinctionist
when you encounter any A and eventually you'll get them.  Sunsword
is an eternal light source when wielded and that's an advantage
that's worth killing Angels for more than just the experience.

There are 2 chaotic artifacts that non-chaotics can get easily if
they don't care about unrestricting the associated skills.  Name
the right type of weapon.  Chaotics aren't restricted from naming,
they can just also get them from sacraficing.

Since archeologists can become Expert at saber, they should use any
silver saber they encounter even if it takes killing a ton of
captains for the 50-50 chance of silver-saber/log-sword weapons
issued to captains.  Getting Werebane as a gift is gravy for an
archeologist.  But you have it so may as well use it enough to
advance saber to Expert.

Vorpal Blade and Fire Brand aren't shabby.  Sure, you want Frost
Brand for later, but before Genhome Firey works as well as Frosty.
Use it at least enough to advance to Basic in long sword.

On the armor, you should have been able to get a better assortment
than just GDSM in the mines.  Using the altar to B/U/C check all
of the dwarvish stuff and trying on all non-cursed should have
given you most stuff +1 or better.

